  "body": "Conditional candidate **\u03ba = 0.001676332167598458**, an exact-profile gain of **0.01558901%** over PR1274's 0.001676070884699375. Compose a second helper-donor cold kernel, pivot 543, with Jeremy Kothe's pivot 531 construction at `336d0ee3ea8026f9388ccafee91c923a434d0328`.\n\n**Local verification completed.** Both full words passed independent rational scalar/frame audits, fresh sequential native transport, ledger, local replay, wrapper and exact phase checks. The standalone package explicitly reused those just-completed, word-bound native runs while repeating all local controls and strict global admission. Two exact moment engines and all 47 outer inequalities pass. Hosted CI is reported separately.\n\nThe frozen constructor reproduces the inherited 159,840 owner roles and dispatch from the final provider interfaces. Re-bound PLAN/SPEC, emitted controller, exact invoice and strict assembly pass. Rejected controls: 12 new pivot-543 mutations, 20 inherited fusion, 8 X54, 8 flow, 114 admission, 15 controller, 12 bit, and 8 independent owner controls. Both words pass the retained leaver-premise checker. The independent owner audit reconstructs source-event windows, checks ordered widths, common ports/centre frames, family noncollision and pending-child axes.\n\nReproduce with `python3 -B research/global-mixed-k531-k543/verify.py --work /absolute/new/output-directory`. Default runs fresh sequential native replay for both words. Explicit `--base-native-from` / `--extra-native-from` reuse checks raw-word identity and all required completed native stages. Requires Python 3.11+, C++ compiler and Boost; no solver or network. Parent geometry and analytic/theorem interfaces remain explicitly inherited, not rebuilt from the original paper. Vendored predecessor receipts retain their original scope; root CLAIM/VALIDATION apply to this composition.\n\nRelative to the pinned PR1274 words, remove B[486], B[520], B[794]; insert 641 += 4*543 immediately before B[160], undo it before B[161], insert 367 -= 543 before B[488], and restore 367 += 543 at the end of early_cleanup. Frozen old/new-key recipes include the jointly optimized frames. Both complete words and parent inputs are committed, so each word can be reconstructed with build_word.py.\n\nBase profile: H1=2352, H2=504, H3=412, H4=130, H5=82, H8=8.\nExtra profile: H1=2344, H2=512, H3=416, H4=126, H5=82, H8=8.\nUse the inherited 125 base / 208 extra allocation and idle H1=2, H48=11374. Aggregate: H1=781554, H2=169496, H3=138028, H4=42458, H5=27306, H8=2664, H48=11374; live=33152, width=73, deficit=11840. Provider interface and hosting compatibility pass the bound local and strict global admission checks.\n\nPR1280 reports a larger 0.001676377648122875 by adding the PR1268 idle overlay. That is not counted as an independently verified comparator here: a separate compressed stream-operator audit has counterexamples for the inherited PR1268 overlay; exact PR1280 composition has not been independently replayed. No claim to exceed that larger unverified number is made.\n\nConditional finite construction only. All-size compiler, common-label/mutable-source realization, whole-call hosting, precision/tape, exact recovery, analytic transfer, PR559 recurrence correction and PR589 bit H1-H5 assumptions remain. No unconditional theorem, full Lean certification, or global packing claim.\n\nCredit: Jeremy Kothe / PR1274 for the exact helper-donor mechanism; Rohan Arun / PR1218 and PR1207 for the mixed X54 fusion construction; Jeremy Diviney / PR1193 for global flow and regular matching; Thomas DiFiore / PR1148, chafreaky / PR1196, Marius-Paul Dumitrean / PR1195, and the retained PR564/571/589/645 lineage. Prepared by Rohan Arun with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n- Independently review the complete conditional composition. First step: run the frozen package with fresh native providers; blocker: all-size compiler and analytic transfer obligations remain inherited.\n- Search further cold pivots for independent helper-donor relations. First step: exact sensitivity relations in this admitted chronology; blocker: any prospective saving must retain scalar endpoints, frames and hosting.\n",
